{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And He afflicted you.</b> On the way. As it is said: ״ענה בדרך כחי קצר ימי״." "<b>And He made you hunger.</b> In that He did not give you food except for the portion of each day, and this is [a form of] hunger, as the Sages said: one who has bread in his basket is not like one who does not." "<b>That He might make you know that not by bread alone.</b> And do not place your trust in bread and in foods, for by all that comes forth from the mouth of HaShem does man live — by all His commandments and statutes that came forth from His mouth does man live, and they give you life in this world and in the world to come."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {0 "The citation appears to be from Deuteronomy 2:7 but is quoted here with spelling variants (ענה for לא חסר, כחי for כחי); rendered as it stands."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:00:38.891839769Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}